# Compiled Python bytecode caches: interpreter-specific, never meant to ship.
# This file alone does NOT keep them out. package.json's "files" allow-list wins over it: with
# npm 10, a checkout that had run the tests packed 59 scripts/__pycache__/*.pyc files (#467 A222).
# The exclusion that works is the negated entries at the end of "files" ("!**/__pycache__/**",
# "!**/*.pyc", "!**/*.pyo"); tests/release_check.sh fails a tarball that still has one. These
# lines stay for an npm that does apply them.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
